  <h2>Do you need a new logo, or just a Google fix?</h2>
  <p>
    Often it is the Google fix. If your category, photos and basics are wrong, sorting those can get
    the phone going again without spending a cent on design. But if you are already booking steady
    work, or launching something you intend to grow, the brand is worth doing early. It ends up on
    your vans, your shirts, your site and your ads, and replacing it later, once people already know
    you, is expensive and messy.
  </p>
  <p>
    We treat branding the same way as the rest of the marketing: who you are up against, what the
    customer is worried about, and how fast they understand you. Not what looks good on the workshop
    wall. We design for the moment a homeowner opens the door, then carry the same look through your
    website and Google profile so it all reads as one company.
  </p>
